Hi @jasonbraley,

Thank you for this report.

A similar issue has been already reported #61.  In I2C memory mode, once memory address written, the device should resend one start bit before switching to read mode. Calling HAL_I2C_Mem_Read_IT() generates multiple start bits, resulting in the slave device answering with a NAK which explains the numerous interruptions generated.

