I have get rid of UserTxBufferFS in my application and don't want any extra buffer of transmission (which I guess was the intention of this buffer, i.e. an intermediate storage). Please note that in:
```
uint8_t CDC_Transmit_FS(uint8_t* Buf, uint16_t Len)
{
  uint8_t result = USBD_OK;
  /* USER CODE BEGIN 7 */
  USBD_CDC_HandleTypeDef *hcdc = (USBD_CDC_HandleTypeDef*)hUsbDeviceFS.pClassData;
  if (hcdc->TxState != 0){
    return USBD_BUSY;
  }
  USBD_CDC_SetTxBuffer(&hUsbDeviceFS, Buf, Len);
  result = USBD_CDC_TransmitPacket(&hUsbDeviceFS);
  /* USER CODE END 7 */
  return result;
}
```

The content of the user buffer (Buf), needs to be valid until USB driver has sent the data. However there is no function to check or wait for this. I did like this in my application:
```
static uint8_t CdcTransmitOngoing()
{
    USBD_CDC_HandleTypeDef *hCdc = (USBD_CDC_HandleTypeDef*)hUsbDeviceFS.pClassData;
    return (hCdc->TxState != 0) ? 1 : 0;
}

static void CdcTransmit(uint8_t* Buf, uint16_t Len)
{
    USBD_CDC_SetTxBuffer(&hUsbDeviceFS, Buf, Len);
    USBD_CDC_TransmitPacket(&hUsbDeviceFS);
    while (CdcTransmitOngoing())
        ; // Need to wait until the buffer is read out
}
```
PS. _The standard case is to enqueue data from user application side which then transparently gets sent out whenever the USB becomes free._ Might not be a good idea in this type of devices, since it require extra memory and copy of data. In my use case I actually will use nearly all RAM in the device for a big buffer that shall be sent over USB. I have no space to copy this data to an USB intermediate buffer.

